1
00:00:16,480 --> 00:01:49,380
 Stars, galaxy, in astral seas above, on cosmic paths we'll trace, man, silver wings, liberty, is such a wonder thing, behind us all, come see, come take your place, we're leaving soon for-

2
00:01:49,380 --> 00:02:04,190
 Only this old crate is going to take us into space, in this thing we won't make it.

3
00:02:05,020 --> 00:02:08,800
 Look, I happen to be a fully qualified space pilot, Murdoch.

4
00:02:09,060 --> 00:02:11,820
 And a space pilot who knows his way around the galaxies too.

5
00:02:12,650 --> 00:02:18,920
 Hey, it's one of these pebbles here that crashed into our ancestors' spaceship and made them make a surprise visit to our planet.

6
00:02:19,120 --> 00:02:23,070
 We're close to the spot we want, but this is only the first stage of our journey.

7
00:02:38,670 --> 00:02:56,020
 They'll detect our presence here, won't they?

8
00:02:56,330 --> 00:02:58,590
 Maybe not, with all the asteroids in the region.

9
00:02:59,210 --> 00:03:02,250
 One blip more or less on a radar screen won't attract any attention.

10
00:03:02,430 --> 00:03:05,610
 Take my word for it. Certainly not at this distance. It's a million to one.

11
00:03:05,950 --> 00:03:09,330
 At this distance. But sooner or later, we'll have to go down and land.

12
00:03:10,170 --> 00:03:13,770
 You know, there is one thing that I've been wondering. What is all this laughing?

13
00:03:14,050 --> 00:03:15,910
 Curious behavior, how do your circuits work?

14
00:03:16,180 --> 00:03:18,650
 Aha, that, my squeaky friend, is the question.

15
00:03:19,240 --> 00:03:23,520
 Laughter is the one thing that makes humans different from all other creatures in the universe.

16
00:03:24,300 --> 00:03:27,330
 So, you'd like to know how we'll land.

17
00:03:27,660 --> 00:03:32,830
 We're not going directly to Yama, because if we tried, we would be disintegrated quicker than you could say,

18
00:03:33,110 --> 00:03:34,810
 so long, it's been good to know you.

19
00:03:34,810 --> 00:03:42,290
 Close to Yama, in among the asteroids, I have another base, all equipped, another helicar, hidden away from our enemies.

20
00:03:42,680 --> 00:03:45,460
 Not many patrols go that way. I know the area well.

21
00:03:46,310 --> 00:03:50,510
 When we're ready, we'll have to sit tight, cool it, till one of their helicar patrols comes by.

22
00:03:52,160 --> 00:03:59,100
 It's going to take a lot of patience.

23
00:04:00,440 --> 00:04:03,610
 Okay, their patrol is entering our sector. We can go in.

24
00:04:10,130 --> 00:04:14,480
 They're trading the planet's atmosphere.

25
00:04:20,650 --> 00:04:21,870
 Helicars are spreading out.

26
00:04:22,170 --> 00:04:23,840
 Now I start jamming their circuit.

27
00:04:25,030 --> 00:04:28,700
 Taking a chance, but subtlety isn't their strong point.

28
00:04:29,310 --> 00:04:32,000
 After all, all they are is a lot of junk.

29
00:04:35,560 --> 00:04:37,110
 Take it from me.

30
00:04:37,660 --> 00:04:40,560
 Wolves are around. The only safe place is around the wolves.

31
00:04:40,740 --> 00:04:41,850
 Can't beat them? Join them.

32
00:04:41,850 --> 00:04:45,290
 From a distance, you'd say that's a man's head they've made up there.

33
00:04:45,710 --> 00:04:46,900
 That's what it is.

34
00:04:47,290 --> 00:04:51,310
 It's the machine's homage to their god, their master, their creator.

35
00:04:51,720 --> 00:04:52,980
 The brilliant Dr. Chivas.

36
00:04:53,590 --> 00:04:54,140
 He's mad.

37
00:04:58,660 --> 00:05:02,540
 Nobody spotted us. We look like everyone else.

38
00:05:29,490 --> 00:05:38,200
 So, first, what do you say? Aren't you a creep here?

39
00:05:38,470 --> 00:05:41,700
 Of course, Maestro, I agree entirely. Your design was perfect.

40
00:05:41,950 --> 00:05:43,510
 But we are not on a pleasure cruise.

41
00:05:43,890 --> 00:05:46,190
 Unfortunately, we're here on much more serious business.

42
00:05:49,530 --> 00:06:04,700
 In my opinion, you can't succeed in your struggle unless you have outside help.

43
00:06:04,700 --> 00:06:09,090
 And I assure you, your courage and that of your men is not in question.

44
00:06:09,420 --> 00:06:11,540
 But I agree with our young friend here.

45
00:06:12,250 --> 00:06:14,810
 The ones in the castle are well entrenched.

46
00:06:15,460 --> 00:06:20,370
 Granted, but here we have forces far greater than the scattered units you encountered on Apis.

47
00:06:20,730 --> 00:06:22,530
 It was just one of those units that found you.

48
00:06:23,050 --> 00:06:24,730
 And what is your plan of attack?

49
00:06:25,460 --> 00:06:28,380
 A great mass of their forces will be pulled away on the mission.

50
00:06:28,730 --> 00:06:30,800
 It's then that we'll siege the base and destroy it.

51
00:06:30,840 --> 00:06:32,560
 And then they will return.

52
00:06:32,990 --> 00:06:33,810
 We'll destroy them.

53
00:06:33,910 --> 00:06:36,210
 You won't destroy the whole lot. No sense in dreaming.

54
00:06:36,450 --> 00:06:39,380
 You'll manage to rebuild the base. You won't defeat them all like that.

55
00:06:39,380 --> 00:06:43,860
 Perhaps not, but our task for the present isn't necessarily to defeat them,

56
00:06:43,980 --> 00:06:45,740
 but to keep hope alive in the hearts of men.

57
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:48,200
 Otherwise, all humankind will revert to barbarism.

58
00:06:48,390 --> 00:06:49,240
 Very well, Powers.

59
00:06:49,420 --> 00:06:51,740
 Our young friend has come to contribute to that hope.

60
00:06:52,420 --> 00:06:54,060
 Will you agree to help him?

61
00:06:54,360 --> 00:06:55,470
 Yes, Omega.

62
00:06:56,020 --> 00:06:57,200
 It's really true.

63
00:06:57,560 --> 00:06:59,890
 We have a chance of crushing these monsters forever.

64
00:07:00,310 --> 00:07:01,610
 Captain, we are all with you.

65
00:07:02,060 --> 00:07:04,550
 We all welcome you to our headquarters and to our cause.

66
00:07:05,890 --> 00:07:12,180
 I refuse to speak in the presence of the special representative from Cassiopeia.

67
00:07:12,670 --> 00:07:14,420
 He is human, as are you.

68
00:07:14,930 --> 00:07:15,870
 Yes, I refuse.

69
00:07:16,220 --> 00:07:19,000
 Being telepathic is a matter of sensitivity, that's all.

70
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:23,320
 What I can see in him is so evil, so utterly contaminated, he gives me cold shivers.

71
00:07:23,760 --> 00:07:25,860
 He's filled with hate, jealousy, evil.

72
00:07:26,240 --> 00:07:29,220
 I would rather be telepathically blind than see what I do in him.

73
00:07:29,300 --> 00:07:30,320
 I prefer you to him.

74
00:07:30,690 --> 00:07:32,970
 For what reason do you refuse to help us, then?

75
00:07:33,310 --> 00:07:36,060
 We want to avoid using harsh techniques with you.

76
00:07:36,320 --> 00:07:38,760
 We hold you in very high esteem. You must realize that.

77
00:07:38,940 --> 00:07:40,900
 Go on. Tell us what your power is.

78
00:07:41,210 --> 00:07:42,680
 How does one learn it?

79
00:07:42,900 --> 00:07:44,880
 What training is necessary to succeed?

80
00:07:45,180 --> 00:07:48,440
 I've already told you all I know, all I can say.

81
00:07:48,440 --> 00:07:52,140
 I have no idea where the faculty comes from. Why won't you understand?

82
00:07:52,340 --> 00:07:54,180
 How can we understand what you say?

83
00:07:54,440 --> 00:07:59,370
 You say it is all a question of sensitivity, only we have analyzed the human brain,

84
00:07:59,630 --> 00:08:01,740
 and we can locate no center of feelings.

85
00:08:02,020 --> 00:08:05,480
 Knowledge is stored using crystals in large carbon-based molecules.

86
00:08:05,830 --> 00:08:10,150
 It follows that we humanoids with such structures must respond as humans in this, too.

87
00:08:10,210 --> 00:08:11,990
 I'll say again what I've always said.

88
00:08:12,210 --> 00:08:16,090
 Those powers in me that interest you are not something I've learned, something mechanical.

89
00:08:16,090 --> 00:08:19,690
 It's entirely a matter of sensitivity, a gift, perhaps.

90
00:08:19,690 --> 00:08:25,790
 Beings, individuals mass-produced on an assembly line or chemically cultivated can never possess those powers.

91
00:08:25,790 --> 00:08:27,400
 We would like to know why.

92
00:08:27,400 --> 00:08:30,650
 There is no way that I can help you to process true feelings.

93
00:08:30,650 --> 00:08:31,850
 We do not believe you.

94
00:08:31,850 --> 00:08:53,130
 You insist on hiding your secret from us.

95
00:08:53,130 --> 00:09:23,000
 Little ages around here.

96
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:26,870
 See? Ancient craft. That's all we are allowed to do.

97
00:09:26,870 --> 00:09:30,010
 It's easier to dominate populations who have no knowledge.

98
00:09:30,010 --> 00:09:32,110
 These robots are all rejects of the factory.

99
00:09:32,110 --> 00:09:33,570
 People pick him up and make him work.

100
00:09:33,830 --> 00:09:34,670
 Use him as servants.

101
00:09:35,030 --> 00:09:36,150
 Watch out for that little one.

102
00:09:36,450 --> 00:09:37,970
 He's one of the spies I told you about.

103
00:09:38,130 --> 00:09:38,930
 He sees all.

104
00:09:42,680 --> 00:10:06,070
 It's about time that I got rid of this straight jacket.

105
00:10:07,360 --> 00:10:09,670
 Now we have proof positive.

106
00:10:09,810 --> 00:10:12,970
 Your friend Psyche is indeed being held prisoner in the castle.

107
00:10:13,310 --> 00:10:14,370
 Look through the penetroscope.

108
00:10:14,980 --> 00:10:15,880
 Bit of luck.

109
00:10:16,080 --> 00:10:18,100
 Might catch a glimpse of her passing in front of the window.

110
00:10:18,810 --> 00:10:20,440
 Psyche, she's alive.

111
00:10:20,440 --> 00:10:22,520
 How can we get her out of there, Commander?

112
00:10:22,980 --> 00:10:24,220
 We can't, I'm sorry.

113
00:10:24,910 --> 00:10:26,400
 You can see for yourself.

114
00:10:32,260 --> 00:10:33,840
 Uh-oh, a Nautilus from Cassiopeia.

115
00:10:34,380 --> 00:10:39,190
 Yes, they are the only visitors from other worlds, only them.

116
00:10:39,680 --> 00:10:41,320
 Men who are allies of the machines.

117
00:10:41,860 --> 00:10:44,460
 You see that large building running alongside the spaceport?

118
00:10:44,770 --> 00:10:49,200
 That's their mass production unit, and below it is their control center, their headquarters.

119
00:10:49,720 --> 00:10:51,510
 That is what we must destroy.

120
00:10:51,920 --> 00:10:56,850
 Now take a look at their defenses, the encircling wall reinforced with the powerful force fields.

121
00:10:57,190 --> 00:10:57,930
 See those domes?

122
00:10:58,310 --> 00:11:00,490
 They're cybernetic watchdogs, octopeds.

123
00:11:00,850 --> 00:11:05,470
 Their rays destroy mercilessly, instantly, anyone who dares penetrate into the forbidden zone.

124
00:11:05,470 --> 00:11:07,810
 And if their tentacles get you, it's worse than death.

125
00:11:07,910 --> 00:11:08,810
 It's permanent paralysis.

126
00:11:09,210 --> 00:11:11,050
 Don't they ever switch off their field of force?

127
00:11:11,290 --> 00:11:12,530
 Don't they ever open a door in the wall?

128
00:11:13,090 --> 00:11:14,270
 Yes, sometimes they do.

129
00:11:14,430 --> 00:11:17,000
 They cut the field in open exits to let patrols out

130
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:18,580
 when there is some disturbance in the city.

131
00:11:18,760 --> 00:11:20,180
 Usually it's only for an instant or two.

132
00:11:20,240 --> 00:11:22,730
 In that case, the problem is simple.

133
00:11:22,890 --> 00:11:24,450
 The doors in the wall, the field of force,

134
00:11:24,510 --> 00:11:27,110
 all that must be minutely and perfectly programmed

135
00:11:27,110 --> 00:11:27,990
 and coded, of course.

136
00:11:28,290 --> 00:11:30,410
 Well, all we have to do is decode the whole business.

137
00:11:30,730 --> 00:11:32,930
 That way we can switch off the field, open the doors.

138
00:11:33,360 --> 00:11:34,500
 What kind of idea is that?

139
00:11:34,500 --> 00:11:38,810
 Miles play. These humans, what poverty of imagination. I don't believe it.

140
00:11:39,050 --> 00:11:43,770
 Sometimes I wonder how they ever had the intelligence to create such an extraordinary individual as yours truly.

141
00:11:44,410 --> 00:11:48,780
 Well, back to work. Here's what I suggest. First of all, they have to come out of their fortress there.

142
00:11:49,010 --> 00:11:50,360
 They have to switch off the field of force.

143
00:11:52,460 --> 00:11:55,880
 You will be pleased to learn that you are going to have a visit from one of your own kind.

144
00:11:56,020 --> 00:11:57,420
 The one you will see is a man.

145
00:11:57,960 --> 00:12:01,350
 We want to amuse you. We are sure you will be amused.

146
00:12:03,450 --> 00:12:05,860
 You're from Cassiopeia.

147
00:12:07,040 --> 00:12:08,290
 You're a shaman.

148
00:12:08,290 --> 00:12:13,600
 We know your conversation with him will yield more than your conversation with us.

149
00:12:13,600 --> 00:12:17,200
 I am quite certain our meeting will yield results. I needn't try to hide it.

150
00:12:17,200 --> 00:12:21,700
 I'm a telepathic being, an ESP, adept if you prefer, the highest developed on Cassiopeia.

151
00:12:21,700 --> 00:12:24,200
 I am master of the fourth category, and what are you, young lady?

152
00:12:24,200 --> 00:12:28,710
 Me? Oh, I'm not in any category. I've never studied any of this.

153
00:12:28,710 --> 00:12:41,770
 I understand. You're trying to dominate my will.

154
00:12:41,770 --> 00:12:45,270
 You have considerable power for a non-professional, we shall see.

155
00:12:45,270 --> 00:12:59,150
 I see you're not afraid of white mice, eh?

156
00:12:59,150 --> 00:13:26,570
 Next. Now the stakes will be higher. Ready?

157
00:13:30,230 --> 00:13:39,130
 You know how to defend yourself.

158
00:13:39,980 --> 00:13:42,600
 We shall meet again soon. Very soon.

159
00:13:46,890 --> 00:13:52,050
 Forces of evil to triumph. They will not triumph.

160
00:13:52,760 --> 00:13:54,860
 Your ordeal will end soon.

161
00:13:55,540 --> 00:13:57,750
 Go on. I can't go on anymore.

162
00:13:58,240 --> 00:13:59,610
 Your friends are near.

163
00:14:26,770 --> 00:14:31,300
 Metro's running things from the roof.

164
00:14:33,810 --> 00:14:39,120
 Didn't work. Nobody's perfect. The field of force wasn't switched off.

165
00:14:39,340 --> 00:14:41,480
 And they used helio cars and jumped right over it.

166
00:14:41,710 --> 00:14:42,600
 All that bad luck.

167
00:14:43,130 --> 00:14:46,580
 We'll need to find another plan, so they'll have to come out using an exit.

168
00:14:46,580 --> 00:15:01,790
 In the name of Cassiopeia, victory is at hand.

169
00:15:08,270 --> 00:15:13,970
 Gentlemen, as for the little troublemaker from Omega, I leave it up to your discretion.

170
00:15:14,050 --> 00:15:16,590
 Honored consul, we may assure you she will be dealt with.

171
00:15:17,410 --> 00:15:18,990
 Cassiopeia gives you full authority.

172
00:15:19,510 --> 00:15:19,830
 Hi!

173
00:15:20,230 --> 00:15:25,510
 Hi, idiot.

174
00:15:25,920 --> 00:15:27,080
 Now it's our turn.

175
00:15:56,880 --> 00:16:11,640
 It's as if our people will all make it back to safety.

176
00:16:12,490 --> 00:16:16,230
 I hope that your friend on the roof did exactly what he said he'd do unless he's all talk.

177
00:16:17,710 --> 00:16:18,910
 Well, that's that.

178
00:16:19,150 --> 00:16:20,530
 As I thought, nothing to it.

179
00:16:20,940 --> 00:16:24,400
 The only problem now is I have to play Santa Claus to rejoin the others.

180
00:16:24,400 --> 00:16:24,960
 Oh, well.

181
00:16:25,120 --> 00:16:25,940
 Ho, ho, ho.

182
00:16:26,060 --> 00:16:29,880
 When you come down to it, my life is no picnic.

183
00:16:30,440 --> 00:16:32,820
 The force field is sub-nucleonic type.

184
00:16:32,960 --> 00:16:37,380
 By vibration of particles, a discontinuity is created in the constituent structure of the matter.

185
00:16:37,780 --> 00:16:39,010
 Quite an easy technique.

186
00:16:39,670 --> 00:16:41,550
 Yes, easy, Mr. Simple.

187
00:16:41,690 --> 00:16:44,530
 But did you work out the code that deactivates the field of force?

188
00:16:44,790 --> 00:16:47,630
 Haven't we known each other long enough for you to trust me?

189
00:16:47,730 --> 00:16:50,070
 I think you could have guessed that I would have it.

190
00:16:50,130 --> 00:16:50,950
 Of course I do.

191
00:16:50,950 --> 00:16:55,250
 That leaves us with the only tiny problem, those ridiculous tentacle ray machines.

192
00:16:55,740 --> 00:16:57,960
 I see a new alternative. We must attack them.

193
00:16:58,200 --> 00:16:59,800
 Are you ready to risk the lives of your men?

194
00:17:00,100 --> 00:17:02,280
 Mine are determined. They're ready for anything.

195
00:17:02,750 --> 00:17:07,130
 Mine are trained and ready to enter into the struggle wherever and whenever they are needed.

196
00:17:07,290 --> 00:17:08,410
 What's your plan, Captain?

197
00:17:08,990 --> 00:17:13,410
 Once the octopods are out of the way, Metro and I will all alone go past the field of force.

198
00:17:13,730 --> 00:17:16,270
 Then we'll jump over the wall and get into the castle.

199
00:17:16,590 --> 00:17:19,650
 And it all has to go so fast they believe it was only a short circuit.

200
00:17:19,650 --> 00:17:22,590
 When we're inside, Metro and I, we know our way around.

201
00:17:22,790 --> 00:17:24,610
 It's only an idea, but what about this?

202
00:17:27,020 --> 00:17:36,870
 That's all there is to it.

203
00:17:37,900 --> 00:17:39,640
 It's serious, Metro.

204
00:17:39,910 --> 00:17:41,570
 They could see you and shoot you down.

205
00:17:41,770 --> 00:17:43,020
 Wouldn't get us very far.

206
00:17:43,360 --> 00:17:44,700
 Let's go over it again, huh?

207
00:17:44,820 --> 00:17:48,940
 If everything goes well, we'll use the underground passages to get back to your ship,

208
00:17:49,050 --> 00:17:51,840
 then to the asteroids, and we inform Omega, who return here in strength.

209
00:17:52,090 --> 00:17:55,280
 I agree, but on the condition that I go with you into the castle.

210
00:17:55,980 --> 00:17:59,830
 For Doc, the two of us, Saki and I, we can fly out on Metro if necessary.

211
00:18:00,090 --> 00:18:02,010
 He can't carry three. It wouldn't work.

212
00:18:02,220 --> 00:18:04,430
 It's time you learned one thing, young Captain.

213
00:18:04,570 --> 00:18:06,790
 I, too, have been around. Take it or leave it.

214
00:18:06,790 --> 00:18:10,120
 And if anything happens to you, who would pilot your ship out of here?

215
00:18:10,200 --> 00:18:13,240
 Why, you, Captain, you are a qualified space pilot, if I recall.

216
00:18:13,980 --> 00:18:22,730
 This voyage is endless, goes on forever.

217
00:18:23,050 --> 00:18:26,450
 With a light cruiser-type Cobra, we would be there already, Maestro.

218
00:18:26,650 --> 00:18:29,310
 My dear sir, this new ship is worth a hundred Cobras.

219
00:18:29,590 --> 00:18:31,010
 I'll go farther, worth a thousand.

220
00:18:31,230 --> 00:18:35,390
 Don't you realize you're in an impregnable fortress, and according to Piero, uh...

221
00:18:35,390 --> 00:18:35,850
 Exactly.

222
00:18:36,320 --> 00:18:38,310
 Colonel, Nebula 6188.

223
00:18:38,310 --> 00:18:42,140
 I just received a report that we are now approaching Nebula 6188.

224
00:18:43,020 --> 00:18:44,560
 That means we have eight hours to go.

225
00:18:45,290 --> 00:18:48,410
 Why don't you sleep? Who knows what awaits us.

226
00:18:48,570 --> 00:18:51,790
 No, but I'm not tired. Why such a voyage with this kind of comfort?

227
00:18:52,030 --> 00:18:56,290
 Believe me, Pierre, here you have easily the finest craft ever created. You'll see that in time.

228
00:18:56,490 --> 00:18:58,770
 Only is it going to be good enough in a fight.

229
00:18:59,290 --> 00:19:03,860
 It will have to be good if we're to believe Piero's report. He talks of the most powerful ships ever seen.

230
00:19:04,720 --> 00:19:07,260
 I think we can put that down to youthful enthusiasm.

231
00:19:07,260 --> 00:19:12,760
 I ask you, monstrous craft, hundreds of thousands of tons, really, what sort of engines could ever get him off the ground?

232
00:19:13,180 --> 00:19:14,820
 Yes, you're right. I, too, wonder.

233
00:19:15,320 --> 00:19:19,600
 Even if General Grouchly is ready to make his assault, his technology isn't up to that.

234
00:19:20,090 --> 00:19:25,840
 Could it be some unknown beings on an undiscovered planet there ahead in the region of Scorpio?

235
00:19:26,330 --> 00:19:29,490
 It's so difficult to think so, and yet, who knows?

236
00:19:29,870 --> 00:19:31,450
 You know what he's like, Maestro.

237
00:19:31,630 --> 00:19:33,870
 I wouldn't say that Piero tends to exaggerate.

238
